# Two real CLI scans over labeled imported contexts; no provider or target code execution.
name: Recorded context comparison across immutable revisions
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR
env: KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_comparison.py @TMP_TARGET @ART/fixture
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | shell-ready
submit: runs diff context-base context-later
require-live-snap: 25 Threat model: changed | recorded-contexts
require-live-snap: 30 status: completed -> completed | loaded-contexts
expect: Base threat model: tm_
expect: Later threat model: tm_
expect: scan conditions differ
expect: Absence does not establish a fix.
ask: Do the source and threat-model identities make the changed scan conditions clear without implying a finding was fixed?
resize: 80x24
live-snap: narrow-contexts
expect: Threat model: changed
ask: At 80x24, are the source and context values wrapped legibly with the comparison state visible?
nav-mode:
keys: NPage
keys: NPage
live-snap: comparison-details
expect: NOT OBSERVED IN COVERED WORK
ask: Can the operator reach the remaining comparison details and see that unavailable evidence has not established a fix?
keys: PPage
keys: PPage
live-snap: comparison-origin
expect: context-base
expect: context-later
ask: Can the operator return by keyboard to the same run pair after scrolling?
keys: C-c
